[Music]  it's midterm elections in el salvador  this year many people are expected to  vote along party lines  and the new ideas party led by el  salvador's president naib bouquet  is a favorite to win president pukele is  very popular among voters and even  though the president is not on the  ballot  the logic among many here seems to be  that a vote for the president's party  is a vote to support the president's  national agenda  it's important for us to vote i think  president bukele  is very capable he has shown us that he  can make our country succeed  everyone trusts him we know he's going  to do good  last november president bukela's  approval rating was 96 percent  according to a gallup poll and  congressional candidates are hoping to  ride on the coattails of that popularity  and seize a congressional majority for  the president's party  some analysts however say controlling a  majority of seats in the salvadoran  congress  would further consolidate the powers of  the presidency  a slippery slope toward the politics of  the 1970s and 80s  when the president held absolute power  if you listen to the propaganda from the  new ideas party the only thing they're  proposing  is to help the president govern they'll  exist only to carry out the interests of  the president  they are offering no other pragmatic  legislative purpose  since becoming president in 2019  nadipuquel's popularity has only grown  much of this is due to the success of  his government's anti-violence  initiative  which cut homicides in the country by  almost half  however buchela has also clashed with  political opponents  and has been criticized by human rights  groups who have accused him of having an  authoritarian streak  pointing to the treatment of gang  members in the nation's prisons  and last year bugele drew harsh  criticism after he brought  armed soldiers into el salvador's  national congress building to pressure  lawmakers into approving  a new security law  is someone who does not respect the rule  of law he disrespects opponents  disrespects the national and  international press and disrespects  every person who has the courage to  oppose him  some political observers say sunday's  municipal and congressional elections  could prove consequential for the future  of el salvador's democracy  opinion polls project the president's  new ideas party  will win between 43 and 56 of the 84  seeds up for grabs  in el salvador's congress manuel rapalo  al jazeera

